{% set slug = config.engine.slug %}
## Splice point 1: NO CMAKE EDIT IS REQUIRED to install this bundle's descriptors.
##
## Place the authored files under the root the bundle targets and the build picks them
## up by directory: for a TEST bundle, under `test_descriptors/<set>/<slug>/`, which
## hkp_wire_pack_target walks and which
## install(DIRECTORY "${HIPKERNELPROVIDER_TEST_DESCRIPTOR_BUILD_DIR}/" ...) installs
## unconditionally under HIPKERNELPROVIDER_ENABLE_TESTS; for a SHIPPED bundle, under
## `descriptors/<producer>/<bundle>/`, reached through the
## HIPKERNELPROVIDER_PRODUCTION_SOURCE_ROOT CACHE PATH, whose default is the in-tree
## E/descriptors/ and which installs under if(TARGET hkp_packaging_product). An author
## who needs a different root overrides that cache variable; they do not add CMake.
##
## The two roots an authored bundle is written under, and the only two an author ever
## repoints: HIPKERNELPROVIDER_PRODUCTION_SOURCE_ROOT for the shipped tree, and
## HIPKERNELPROVIDER_TEST_DESCRIPTOR_SOURCE_ROOT for test_descriptors/.
##
{% if config.is_packaged %}
## This is a PACKAGED bundle, so its descriptors are not read by the runtime loader as
## authored. hkp_pack walks the shipped source root recursively, compiles or lowers
## each UKD, and writes the descriptors into the per-arch tree itself, rewriting
## `kind: {{ config.kernel_source_kind }}` to `kind: kpack` on the way. Installing a
## second, unlowered copy would give the loader a kind it rejects ("no implementation
## yet") -- dropping the pack, then the engine -- so the authored files belong under
## the shipped source root and nowhere else.
##
## Authored subpath (preserved verbatim into the staged and installed trees):
##     {{ config.descriptor_dir }}/
##
## Files placed there by this run:
{% for pack in config.packs %}
##     {{ config.kdp_stem(pack) }}.kdp.json
{% if config.is_multi_pack %}
##     operation_is_{{ pack.discriminator }}.umd.json
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
##     {{ slug }}.kmd.json
##     {{ slug }}.ued.json
##     {{ slug }}.udd.json
{% if config.engine.has_heuristic %}
##     {{ slug }}.uhd.json
{% endif %}
##     kernel_dtype_matches_graph.umd.json
{% else %}
## This is a DIRECT-LOAD bundle: the runtime loader reads these files as authored, out
## of the shard belonging to the set `{{ config.authored_subpath }}`.
## The set is the whole mechanism -- it is a pack target walked by directory, so a
## bundle written into the wrong set installs cleanly and is then invisible to the
## binary meant to read it.
##
## Authored subpath:
##     {{ config.descriptor_dir }}/
##
## Files placed there by this run:
##     {{ slug }}.kmd.json
##     {{ slug }}.ued.json
##     {{ slug }}.udd.json
{% if config.engine.has_heuristic %}
##     {{ slug }}.uhd.json
{% endif %}
##     kernel_dtype_matches_graph.umd.json
{% for pack in config.packs %}
##     {{ config.kdp_stem(pack) }}.kdp.json
{% if config.is_multi_pack %}
##     operation_is_{{ pack.discriminator }}.umd.json
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
